Negative control for the error SCOPE (P1-R13).

Drops the "has already presented" guard, so a row action the API refuses
replaces the whole list with the load-error panel — the defect the operator
drove into: one 409 takes the table, its controls and the user's place in the
list away, with no way back short of a page reload.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: list-surface-error-scope.spec.ts — the cases holding the presented list
on screen through an action failure.

